Reasons of gatewayAPI - 

1 . Ingress has only 2 spec section , 
  a. path 
  b. service 
It lacked canary model of deployment , Web Application Firewall [ WAF ] , Rate limiting , DDoS 
However, these was overcome through annotations but ingress became  very complex. 

	2. It is actually the duty of platform engineer to install ingress Class, however DevOps team too was making the modification of ingress Class in the ingress file. It became confusion .

In order to solve above problems, gatewayAPI came into place. 
Gateway API 
 - gatewayclass resource
 - gateway resource 
 - httproute  resource 


Gateway -  installs  3 custom resources 
 gatewayClass -  It is similar to controller , Defines which controller manages gateways 
  gateway Resource - Defines gatewayclass to be used 
  httpRoute - Defines Routing rules , allows HTTP / HTPPs , Weight based Routing , 
Gateway API - It is a newer version of ingress. 

In ingress, user send a request using http/https , the request reaches to the ingress which is managed by ingress controller. Based on the  rules setup in ingress, the request flows to service and from service to deployment/pods 

Disadvantages of Ingress -

	1. Ingress only support host/path based routing 
	2. Supports HTTP Routing

Ingress --> SVC -->. Pod 
Gateway ---> TLS Route --> SVC. ---> Pod 

We can create TLS Route/ HTTP Route / UDP Route  can be http route. Based on the rule mentioned in the route, it will be redirected to svc and then to pod

Advantages of Gateway - 

	1. Gateway API supports HTTP / HTTPS / TCP / UDP routing 
	2. provides Advanced routing capabilities 
	3. Supports method based , header based routing , Weight based routing , Traffic splitting , query based routing 
	4. Distributed as CRDs [ Custom Resource Definition ]. Benefit of using Custom Resource is we can add lot of features based on our need. 
	
	
Components of Gateway API -
	1. GatewayClass - It is type of load balancing implementation. Defines how a gateway is implemented by a controller. . Gateway class implementation of gateway controller. 
	GatewayClass defines a type of Gateway, but not an actual instance.Eg - nginx
	2. Gateway- Actual Load balancer instance which receives the traffic/request from the outside user & based on the HTTProute it sends the request to the required svc & to pods
	3. HTTPRoute - Routing rules for mapping traffic. Based on http

Gateway receives the HTTP/HTTPs request from external user , Gateway is a implementation class and based on the route configured on the gateway resource  it will redirect to the service and from service to pod 

The Gateway resource is used to define an instance of a Gateway API implementation. It acts as an entry point for traffic into the cluster. GatewayClass defines a type of Gateway, but not an actual instance.

Gateway is layered approach where every component is managed by separate teams - 
Gateway Class - Infra Team
Gateway - Cluster Operator
httpRoute [TCP , UDP, HTTPS , HTTP ] - Application/Development Team 


